-# Design analysis for the combo variant D7/3 + D16/0
-# a) Concrete behavior and trace
-#    - Stage 1 keeps the core b9e38dc0 geometry: detect the wall, infer the opening
-#      direction `rad`, flood the seed inside the funnel, then radiate that fill through
-#      the opening.
-#    - Stage 2 no longer treats extra singleton pixels as shadow-casters. Every extra
-#      non-wall, non-fill singleton is a mover that advances one cell at a time along the
-#      same `rad`.
-#    - If a mover reaches the stage-1 wall+fill sprite, it is absorbed instead of stopping
-#      in front of it. Absorption recolors the whole filled region to that mover's color.
-#      With multiple movers, arrival time is the ray distance to the first hit cell; later
-#      arrivals overwrite earlier recolors, so the last absorber decides the final fill color.
-#    - Small example for `rad = down`: two movers sit above the funnel in different columns.
-#      A near red mover hits after 3 steps, so the filled region becomes red; a farther blue
-#      mover hits after 6 steps, so the same region is recolored blue in the final output.
-#      Any mover whose lane misses the sprite continues to the bottom border as usual.
-# b) Complexity calibration
-#    - The original wall/fill inference is preserved, so the task still has one dominant
-#      large object and one movement direction to read.
-#    - D16/0 is made visible by requiring 2-4 mover singletons per sample, with at least
-#      two absorbed on parallel lanes and at distinct distances. That creates repeated
-#      evidence for "many pixels target one sprite" without introducing multiple competing
-#      pairing rules.
-#    - Optional survivor movers are capped at one or two so movement remains readable and
-#      the core absorption/recolor effect stays central.
-# c) Implicit-assumption audit
-#    - The old shadow logic assumed extra pixels were static blockers. That is invalid now:
-#      extras must be traced as moving entities, and the stage-1 sprite is the obstacle.
-#    - Fill-color detection still assumes the true seed color is the non-wall color closest
-#      to the wall. Generator therefore keeps movers several cells away from the wall.
